{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>Then He grants him favor</b> — the Place [i.e., God]; and <b>He says to the intercessor, 'Redeem him,'</b> like פדהו (redeem him), and it has no parallel in Scripture. Likewise: רטפש [a unique form]. And its meaning is 'soft.'"], :book :job, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 33, :register {:flags {0 ["God"]}}, :notes {0 "The referent of the subject of ויחננו and the object of ויאמר is resolved by reading 'the Place' as an epithet for God; פדעהו is analyzed as a unique form parallel in rarity to רטפש, whose meaning Ibn Ezra glosses as 'soft.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Job -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/eyov/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:04:24.043854343Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}